<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n66343" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέροψ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οπος</span>, ὁ, poet. word, used only in pl. as epith. of
		men, derived by Gramm. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μείρομαι,
		ὄψ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dividing the
				voice</i>, i. e. <i>articulate</i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				11.1.250
			</span></i>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἄνθρωποι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
				</span></i>
			 l.c., <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				109
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. βροτοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.2.285
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μερόπεσσι λαοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					90
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): hence as Subst., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνθρωποι</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Musae.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				13
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				1018
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				1263
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.536
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				418
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.563
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.); a usage satirized by <i><span class="en">Strato Com.,
					1.6</span></i> sq. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in sg. and pl., <i>bee-eater, Merops
				apiaster</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				615b25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.976d
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴροψ</span>.</div>
